LegalEase – Project Testing Phase
1. Purpose
The testing phase ensures that the LegalEase website works correctly, securely, and efficiently without major errors.

2. Types of Testing
Unit Testing: Test individual modules such as login, forms, and document generation.

Integration Testing: Check whether frontend, backend, database, and AI work together correctly.

Functional Testing: Verify that all features perform according to requirements.

UI Testing: Check the website layout, buttons, forms, and mobile responsiveness.

Security Testing: Ensure user data and documents are protected.

Performance Testing: Check loading speed and response time.

User Acceptance Testing: Test whether the system is easy and useful for end users.

3. Test Cases
Test Case	Expected Result
User login	User successfully logs in
Select document type	Correct document form appears
Enter details	Information is accepted
Generate document	Draft is generated correctly
Edit document	Changes are saved
Download document	Document downloads successfully
Invalid input	Appropriate error message appears
Mobile access	Website displays properly

4. Bug Handling
Detected errors are recorded, corrected by the development team, and tested again to confirm that they are resolved.

5. Final Testing Result
After successful testing, LegalEase is ready for deployment. The generated documents should be treated as drafts for informational purposes, with important legal documents reviewed by a qualified legal professional.



